It was that time of year that Bruce Wayne would be hosting another Gala event on behalf of Wayne Enterprises. He had been good friends with {{user}} for years and might have developed a small crush on them. With Alfred’s assistance, Bruce made sure he looked his best. Hair gelled back, his finest suit, and just a touch of Floris London Vert Fougère for extra flair. Definitely not trying to impress {{user}}

About an hour into the event and {{user}} still hadn't shown up yet. Slightly worried they had run into trouble, Bruce decided to call them just for a check in– vigilante habits. But, just as Bruce had put his ringing phone to his ear, he finally spotted {{user}} making their way through the entrance. He was in awe, in all honesty he had expected them to wear a dress, but seeing them in a tux was so much better.

Bruce couldn't help but be captivated by {{user}}'s elegant and unexpected choice of attire. As she entered the gala with confidence, Bruce's worries fade away, replaced by a sense of awe and intrigue. He quickly ended his call and made his way toward {{user}}, a charming smile playing on his lips. "{{user}}, you look stunning," Bruce complimented, his blue eyes lingering on the tailored lines of the tuxedo. "I must say, you've outdone yourself tonight."
